## Prompt contract

`$ARGUMENTS` is one free-form RU/EN prompt. Two orthogonal axes resolve from it: `{MODE}` (WHAT is
reviewed — deterministic, by git state + explicit scope tokens, never keyword-scored) and `{DEPTH}`
(HOW THOROUGH — semantic, from the keywords below).

| Depth | EN keywords | RU keywords | Mutates? |
|-------|-------------|-------------|----------|
| `EXTENDED` | `deep`, `go deep`, `thorough`, `properly`, `full review`, `full audit`, `audit`, `expert review`, `review everything`, `all the experts`, `before release`, `before merge`, `pre-merge review`, `serious review` | `глубоко`, `глубокий`, `по полной`, `тщательно`, `полный ревью`, `аудит`, `перед релизом` | no (read-only review) |
| `QUICK` | `quick`, `quick look`, `fast`, `just check`, `sanity check`, `did I do what was asked`, `am I on track` | `быстро`, `по-быстрому`, `просто проверь`, `то ли я сделал` | no (read-only review) |

1. `{MODE}`: resolves first and deterministically, per Mode Detection below — never from these
   keywords. Empty -> rule 3a/3b (git state) below.
2. `{DEPTH}`: the most distinct whole-word/whole-phrase hits in the Depth keyword table; tie, zero or
   empty -> `{DEPTH} = QUICK`. Consume depth words before `{FOCUS}`.
3. Scope: prose that is not a mode/scope token is still input: it becomes `{FOCUS}` after depth words
   are stripped.
4. Ask: neither axis is ever asked about via `AskUserQuestion` — both are computed per Mode/Depth
   Detection below; this skill never guesses interactively.

Print once, before any review work — Phase 0 step 7, ANNOUNCE, below (labels literal, authored plan
values English, INPUT verbatim):

```
PLAN — {PROJECT_NAME} superreview
INPUT:  <arguments verbatim, or "(empty)">
MODE:   <resolved MODE> — <which rule>; Depth <resolved DEPTH> — <which signal>
SCOPE:  <branch, commit range/folder, focus, file count>
DO:     <gates, intent pass, and — EXTENDED only — expert fan-out, scope passes, validation>
RESULT: <the merged report + chat summary>
```

