## The intent pass — `intent-guard`, spawned at BOTH depths, ALWAYS

`intent-guard` (`.claude/agents/intent-guard.md`) compares **DELIVERED vs ASKED**, outside domain review.
Following an approved plan faithfully can still accumulate drift from the original request.

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Always spawned | at `QUICK` and at `EXTENDED`, in the Phase 2 message — unconditional, NOT chosen by the runtime expert-selection procedure |
| Not a domain expert | never assign it a file group, never count it as the group's owner, never use it as the Phase 3 validator |
| Self-contained | its procedure, evidence budget (<=15 tool calls), tier model, drift classes and output shape live in ITS OWN file. The spawn brief passes context only and NEVER restates them |
| Missing agent | `.claude/agents/intent-guard.md` absent -> the intent pass is `not run`, said so in the ANNOUNCE, the report AND the chat summary, with the advice to regenerate via `/brewcode:superreview-setup`. At `QUICK` that leaves gates only — never report a clean run |

