## Delegation (applies to EVERY Agent this skill spawns)

One subagent = ONE file-group review, ~<=5 files, ~<=10 steps. Split larger groups into N
tasks, all spawned in ONE message; an hour-long agent drifts beyond observation/correction.

Every spawn brief carries six labeled fields, since a subagent starts with an empty context: GOAL (task + why), ROLE (owns, must not touch), SCOPE (paths/commands in and out), CONTEXT (done, by whom, in parallel), CONSUMER (who uses the result + its shape), DONE (acceptance + return: verdict first, evidence, bounded; long output to a file, path returned).

A bare one-line task is never enough. Phase 2 fills these from `references/agent-prompt.md`; Phase 3 fills them
for the validator.

