### Phase 1 — Agent selection (route changed files to domain owners)

> **`{DEPTH}` = `QUICK` -> SKIP this entire phase.** The selected set is exactly `intent-guard`; record
> `Experts: none (QUICK)`. Do NOT add an expert because the diff looks risky — a risky diff is the reason to tell
> the user to re-run deep, not to silently upgrade the depth they chose.

**`EXTENDED` from here to the end of Phase 1.**

Group the `{FILE_LIST}` by path. **Enable ONLY the groups whose files actually changed**: ONE targeted spawn per
relevant group, never a quorum per group plus a separate full standards pass.

{FILE_GROUP_MAP}

> **Total spawns, by depth:**
> `QUICK` = **1** — `intent-guard`, and nothing else.
> `EXTENDED` = `intent-guard` (always) + (NON-EMPTY domain groups) + the TWO scope passes (A diff-side,
> B baseline-side; A alone in `FULL_PROJECT`) + **{0, 1, or 2} general agents (model's call)**.
> `intent-guard` is NOT one of the {0,1,2} general agents and is never traded against them.
> Examples: a tiny single-file tweak = its domain owner + the scope passes; non-trivial logic = domain owner +
> `{VALIDATOR_AGENT}`; multiple domains = both domain owners + `{ARBITER_AGENT}`. A SMALL, single-domain, low-risk
> change MAY skip the general passes — **never a scope pass**: a small diff is exactly where an unnoticed
> foreign-surface edit or an undelivered criterion hides.

> **Test-bloat audit:** when the `tests` group is non-empty, its prompt MUST also carry the test over-proliferation
> block of `references/agent-prompt.md` (`category: test-quality`): fewer tests, never at the cost of isolation,
> speed or real dependencies.

### Phase 2 — ONE parallel fan-out (find candidates)

