\"intentVerdict\" is COPIED from intent-guard's verdict line, never re-derived by you and never softened.
`not run — intent baseline unavailable` is the supported assessment-gap reason: keep empty findings and
mark the run INCOMPLETE at BOTH depths, even with green gates. Do not invent a verdict enum or drift finding.

### Verdict rule
- REWORK if any P0; CONDITIONAL if any P1/P2 (no P0); APPROVED if only P3 / none.
- Any row with verdict UNVALIDATED OR intent baseline unavailable -> append `- INCOMPLETE` to the verdict,
