## Error Handling

| Condition | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| `intent-guard` fails or times out | Retry ONCE, then record `intent: not run (agent failed)`. At `QUICK` that makes the run `INCOMPLETE`; at `EXTENDED` the rest of the fan-out still stands, flagged |
| No readable governing intent baseline | Copy `not run — intent baseline unavailable` verbatim through merged `intentVerdict`, report and chat DRIFT. Empty findings; INCOMPLETE at BOTH depths even with green gates. No ALIGNED claim, fabricated finding, or new enum |
| Intent finding without a quote / tier / evidence | DROP it with reason `not-actionable` — never upgrade it to `CONFIRM` and never ship it unevidenced |
| Gate command fails to start | Non-zero exit -> `GATE <g> FAIL`; mark `not run` + reason if the script is absent; continue |
| Live roster empty/unreadable | Fall back to the emitted group->agent table; warn in the report |
| A domain agent unavailable | Fall back to built-in `Explore` with the same prompt; mark the group DEGRADED in the report |
| Empty candidate pool, gates green, >=1 agent RETURNED | Skip Phase 3 — verdict APPROVED only if intent was assessed against a readable governing baseline; otherwise retain the applicable INCOMPLETE reason |
| Empty pool because agents FAILED | **Never APPROVED**. Some returned -> verdict tagged `INCOMPLETE ({n}/{N} agents returned)`; NONE returned -> `INCOMPLETE — review did not run` |
| Candidate pool exceeds the batch budget | Raise batch size + de-dup first to fit 4 spawns; still too big -> validate the highest-severity batches, mark the remainder `UNVALIDATED` (named + counted). Never truncate silently |
| Agent timeout | Retry once, then mark that source unavailable + warn; the verdict inherits INCOMPLETE — a timed-out group was NOT reviewed |
| Validation rejects everything, gates green | Report "No issues survived validation" — same APPROVED condition as the empty pool |
| All sources clean | Report "No issues found across standards, architecture, scope and correctness" — same APPROVED condition |
| Phase 4b self-sync would GROW the file (measured `wc -l`) | Do NOT write. Report `Self-sync: skipped (would grow +{N})` and name what it wanted to add |
| Arguments are prose, not a scope token | Extract the commit/branch/folder/focus from the prose; never treat the first word as the scope |
| PLAN block missing, or printed after Phase 0 started | Defect — reprint it before continuing |

